# Named Signed Integer Comparison Acceptance

schema_version: 1
directive: `INBOX-33` evidence-ranked successor
target: `x86_64-linux-gnu`
validation_tier: 3
result: pass

The composed selector now admits plain scalar `icmp slt` and `icmp sgt` over
two named i32 or i64 values. Both operands use the existing typed scratch
materialization and register-parametric compare forms. The setcc choice
accounts for the machine layer's AT&T `cmp lhs, rhs` operand order.
`samesign`, i16/i128, immediate operands, unsigned predicates, vectors, and
other comparison shapes remain fail-closed.

Permanent structural coverage proves all four width/predicate combinations
and the exact compare/setcc stream. Near misses keep `samesign` i32 and plain
i16 comparisons at `composed-block-icmp-form`. Executable selector coverage
checks swapped and equal operands at signed boundaries for i32 `slt` and i64
`sgt`, for ten exact calls.

The initial frontier ranking expected `compiler_rt.gedf2.__gedf2`,
`compiler_rt.gesf2.__gesf2`, `compiler_rt.cmpdf2.__cmpdf2`, and
`compiler_rt.comparef.__cmpsf2` to close. Fresh captured IR inspection showed
that each first reaches an earlier `samesign ugt` immediate comparison, so
all four correctly remain fail-closed at `composed-block-icmp-form` and carry
no closure claim.

The exact named relational form instead closes the captured
`compiler_rt.fmod.fmod` and `compiler_rt.fmod.fmodf` rows. A parser/printer
derived module defines only those two z_llvm-emitted bodies. Forty
precomputed-bit native calls match the pinned Zig compiler-rt implementation
over both zero signs, subnormals, normal and extreme finite values, exact and
inexact remainders, infinities, zero divisors, and quiet/signaling NaN
payloads. The emitted object defines both rows and has no relocations.

Fresh report-all advances from 443 selected / 227 emitting / 216 failing to
443 selected / 229 emitting / 214 failing. `fmod` and `fmodf` are the only new
emissions; there are no unproved collateral emissions.

